WEBVTT

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.030
<i>Attention, flying beastman!</i>

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.780
<i>You've entered Japan's airspace</i>
<i>without permission.</i>

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:23.370
<i>Land immediately</i>
<i>and perform immigration procedures.</i>

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:25.870
I'm a wandering albatross.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.750
I'm a protected species according to
the International Migratory Bird Treaty.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.960
<i>The migratory bird treaty</i>
<i>doesn't apply to beastmen.</i>

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.760
<i>Continuing to fly will be considered</i>
<i>a violation of Japan's airspace</i>

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:36.840
<i>and we will attack.</i>

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.390
You have no sense of humor, huh?

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.140
Civil servants sure are square.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.950
<i>You impose your ideas of what's just,</i>
<i>go and feel sorry for me</i>

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.200
<i>and think you have to save me.</i>

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.950
<i>You're only doing it</i>
<i>to make yourself feel better.</i>

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.790
We finally got together again,
and now this! Damn her!

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.680
As Lindbergh said, "My Spirit,
those must be the lights of Paris."

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.680
This is going to be a rough landing.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.730
I am just doing what I feel is right.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.320
So you call that imposing my ideas
on others?

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:12.440
Damn, I really blew it this time.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.610
You're awake?

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.530
Oh, was that my doing?

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:26.200
Yes. You did a magnificent job
of making a hole in the roof.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.910
You should stay in bed.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.790
No, I can't lie in bed
after all the trouble I've caused you.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.170
Anyway, it looks like you're not injured.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.260
Watch out, young lady! A gust is coming!

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.600
Michiru!

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.120
A warm meal sure hits the spot.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.080
Has it been a while since you've eaten?

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.500
I was on the wing for a long time.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.630
You mean
you've escaped here to Anima-City?

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:19.000
Then you need to register as a resident.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.510
I won't be here long.
I'm a wandering albatross, after all.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.260
A wandering albatross?
You're a migratory bird?

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.640
That's right.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.220
I'm so jealous.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.140
Of what?

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.520
You can fly, right?
You can go anywhere you like.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.980
If I could fly, it wouldn't have been
so hard to get here.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.480
Would you like to fly, young lady?

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:41.690
What?

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.950
Yes!

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.700
I looked into
the Church of the Silver Wolf.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:50.200
Until not long ago,
it was a simple folk religion.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.370
About six months ago,

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:56.920
when a man named Cliff Boris joined,
they quickly expanded and became powerful.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.630
What's more, the founder
is a childhood friend of that tanuki girl.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:04.510
Two people with beastman disease,
and they're close friends.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.510
I doubt it's a coincidence.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.140
Don't you agree?

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.100
One caught it from the other.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.810
If that were so,
more people would be infected.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:14.390
That's true.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.480
The mystery grows more puzzling.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.020
I will allow the Church to settle.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.690
If there is a beastman disease,
we should monitor it closely.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.280
<i>Mayor, you have a visitor.</i>

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.740
I don't have any appointments.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.200
<i>Well...</i>

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.750
I'm terribly sorry
for intruding like this.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.670
It's good to see you again,
Mayor Barballet Rosé.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.590
Chairman Alan, what a pleasant surprise.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:45.170
Sorry, but it's my nature to be impulsive.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:51.720
I'm Alan Sylvasta,
Chairman of Sylvasta Pharmaceutical.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:52.850
Nice to meet you.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.310
I'm Shirou Ogami.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.060
Don't you like shaking hands?

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.640
That's right.
I'll get a human scent on me.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.110
Oh, how rude of me.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.980
Mr. Ogami is a consultant to the mayor.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:07.150
He has assisted us
since the founding of Anima-City.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:10.110
Then you're in much
the same position as I am.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.330
I give financial aid,
while you provide expert advice.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.790
You were of assistance
in the Sylvasta Pharmaceutical bombing.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.790
You know about that?

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:21.880
I received a report that you

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:26.550
and your cute assistant girl exposed
Yaba and his cronies' foolish crimes.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.380
"Cute assistant"?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.300
Am I mistaken? That tanuki girl, right?

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.180
She's hardly cute.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.890
I'm just being polite.
No need to take it seriously.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.560
I'm sorry for barging in like this.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:45.320
I heard that the Church of the Silver Wolf
is requesting residency.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:50.200
I think you should turn them down.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:54.660
That would go against the purpose
of this city.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.960
True. Anima-City is a place
for oppressed beastmen to escape to.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.750
By living here, beastmen become acquainted
with human civilization

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.710
and learn how they can coexist
with humans.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.670
I empathize with your beliefs

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.720
and provide you with funding
as the representative of humankind.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.930
That's right. Anima-City does not
turn away beastmen.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:16.930
So why do this?

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:19.930
A whim?

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:24.110
My, what magnificent fangs you have!

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.690
You're quite the wolf beastman.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.070
Ogami!

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.530
I know full well that the young heir

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:33.910
to the Sylvasta Conglomerate
doesn't act merely on a whim.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.990
You give me far too much credit.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:41.790
I simply believe that Anima-City doesn't
need the Church of the Silver Wolf now.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:42.830
Why?

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.670
While beastmen are trying to modernize,

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:49.420
allowing a beastman cult into this city
would have an adverse effect.

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:51.420
It would agitate anti-beastman factions.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.380
I'm sure you've heard.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:57.310
<i>Recently, central figures</i>
<i>in the beastman rights movement,</i>

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:00.640
<i>such as elected officials,</i>
<i>beastman activists, and journalists,</i>

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.060
<i>have been getting shot.</i>

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:06.400
There are reports of unidentified
flying beastmen crossing our borders too.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:09.230
Naturally,
the final decision lies with you.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:14.490
Depending on your decision,
I may need to rethink my position.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:15.950
Is that a threat?

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.410
No, just a piece of advice.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.580
Now that the Medical Center
has no director,

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.580
I'll be taking charge.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:27.880
If possible, I'd like to
continue working with Anima-City.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:29.840
Goodbye.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.890
This feels so nice!

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.010
The winds in this city sure can be fickle.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.060
I've caught it!

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.280
This is amazing!

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.650
How do you catch the wind?

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.450
How do I catch it?

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.370
I just know. I'm used to it.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:00.660
My father taught me about
where the wind comes from

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.330
and how it blows.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.910
His father taught him.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:10.040
Scientifically, there are complex aspects
like humidity and air pressure.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.340
But to beastmen, it's second nature.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.630
It must be nice to be free.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.930
Free, you say?

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.600
It used to be that way.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.350
We're migratory bird beastmen.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:26.270
Like migratory birds, we migrate.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.270
That's how our ancestors lived
for generations.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:32.900
But when beastmen were given
the same rights as humans,

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.860
migration became prohibited.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:37.700
When we cross borders, we need a passport

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.200
and have to go
through immigration procedures.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:42.660
Oh, is that right?

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:46.000
The routes
that our ancestors flew long ago

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.210
are deeply ingrained into our bodies.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.380
We can't go and change them now.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:55.170
<i>Why do we have to change them for humans?</i>

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:58.340
<i>Some of my kind who believed that</i>
<i>have been shot down.</i>

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.720
<i>They called it an illegal border crossing.</i>

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:03.930
You must be kidding.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:07.390
Beastmen must live by
the laws of humans as well.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.360
Are humans really so superior?

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.570
Can I have one of those?

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:18.280
They're only for beastmen.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:20.740
You can tell I'm a human?

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.200
By your scent.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.660
Is that right? Anyway, I'll take one.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.410
Here you go.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.590
You're right.
This isn't for human consumption.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.590
You plan to let
that young kid boss you around?

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:39.010
Don't underestimate him
just because he's young.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:43.260
The Sylvasta Conglomerate
is a distinguished old family from Europe.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:46.640
Alan is regarded as the future
central figure of the conglomerate.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.890
You know that

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:52.650
this city relies on financial aid
from Sylvasta Pharmaceutical.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:54.820
That Church is fishy.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.570
But I hate being bossed around
by humans even more.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.820
I still have to make a decision about it.

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:08.700
Even if it results
in incurring the hatred of beastmen.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.330
<i>The government has confirmed it.</i>

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:15.880
<i>A bird beastman illegally</i>
<i>crossed the border</i>

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.710
<i>and is hiding somewhere within Anima-City.</i>

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:22.970
<i>They say he's most likely</i>
<i>an anti-beastman-rights terrorist.</i>

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:26.720
It appears
what Alan said was no mere threat.

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.360
What is that fool doing?

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:42.070
Okay, our pleasure flight is over,
young lady.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:49.790
Here. This is to pay for the roof repairs.
I'm sorry it's in dollars.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:53.210
-What?
-I doubt I'll still be here tomorrow.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:54.460
This is farewell.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.170
You're leaving already?

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.130
I'm a migratory bird, after all.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:59.670
Oh, I guess so.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:02.840
At least tell me your name.

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:03.970
Pingua.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.640
Farewell, Pingua!

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:14.230
Drop by the next time
you migrate this way!

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:26.410
Where's the bird beastman?

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:28.450
You mean Pingua?

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.080
He left.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:35.330
-What's the problem?
-That guy could be a terrorist.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.920
A terrorist?

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.800
You can't be serious.
He said he's leaving tomorrow.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.550
Then he could be carrying it out tonight.

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:48.140
What's wrong with you?
Pingua is not that kind of person.

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:52.100
You can tell that
after flying around a little together?

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:53.930
That's pretty rude.

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:57.150
Besides, how did you know
we flew together?

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:01.690
I saw you from the city hall
on a carefree flight.

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:04.320
It wasn't carefree!

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.950
Not in the least!
You don't know what it was really like!

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.330
I don't know what?

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.290
I didn't realize that

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:15.960
having human rights doesn't mean happiness
for all beastmen.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.170
The migrant bird problem?

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:19.670
You knew about it?

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.920
Pingua said that
some of his own friends were shot.

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:26.470
Then he has an underlying motive.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:29.390
Why do you only see the negative aspect
of things?

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:33.600
Apparently, an anti-beastman-rights
terrorist is hiding out in Anima-City.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.850
And they're a bird beastman too.

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:39.610
Considering the timing,
I have to suspect him.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:42.320
I don't have time to argue about it.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:45.900
Then find him and clear your suspicions.

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.950
If they can be cleared.

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:49.740
Can't you follow his scent?

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:53.580
The sky is my weakness.
It scatters the scent trails in no time.

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:55.370
Is there any other way?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.210
No, but I have a hunch
about what he's up to.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.540
Wait up!

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:15.810
<i>Mayor Rosé has refused to give</i>
<i>the Church of the Silver Wolf</i>

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:17.810
<i>the right to settle in Anima-City.</i>

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:21.480
<i>She's preparing an alternate settlement</i>
<i>land and negotiating with them.</i>

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:26.070
<i>The mayor stated, "The infrastructure</i>
<i>isn't in place to handle the Church.</i>

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.650
<i>I'd like them to temporarily move</i>

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:31.200
<i>while we prepare</i>
<i>for their eventual acceptance."</i>

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.410
This is what you want?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.660
Yes. It's all going according to plan.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:45.130
Hey! The Church is on the move!

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:46.840
What? Are you serious?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:49.170
That's right! Silver Wolf is leading them!

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.550
Silver Wolf is?

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:57.640
We, the Church of the Silver Wolf,
desired to settle here in Anima-City.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:01.020
However, Mayor Rosé turned us down!

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:04.520
She did it out of concern
for Sylvasta Pharmaceutical.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.610
But we are not fanatics.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:11.160
We merely desire a paradise
for all beastmen.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:15.490
Let us all pray that
all their misconceptions be dispelled.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.500
Let us rejoice!

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:29.170
Silver Wolf is the guardian of beastmen!

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:34.390
May her light forever maintain the peace
of all beastmen!

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.970
The Church is at Medi-Cen.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:42.440
It seems they're aware
of Chairman Alan's interference.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:45.860
It wasn't a divine revelation, was it?

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:49.900
Many people saw him come to the city hall.

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.740
At any rate, contact the police.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:55.030
Just continue observing for now.

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:56.620
No violence.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.140
Okay, let's do this.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:32.950
Who the heck are you?

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:40.240
Nobody gets away with terrorism
in Anima-City!

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.160
I wish you'd quit trying to stop me.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.340
Shirou!

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:53.550
I wish I could fly!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.550
Don't hold this against me, pal!

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:26.500
Let me fly!

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.920
You can fly?

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:33.920
This is my first time!

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.630
-Your first time?
-Yes!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.390
Can you fly above him?

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:40.930
You got it!

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:51.860
Holy cow! Is that even possible?

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:57.490
You won't get away this time.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:12.920
Tanuki girl, huh? You really fooled me.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.760
You were in the military, weren't you?

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:19.430
Yes, I was in the beastman military
when I was younger.

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:24.350
I believed in human rights for beastmen
and fought against anti-beastman radicals.

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:28.850
But I never once expected that to result
in being unable to migrate.

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.600
That's no reason!

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:33.440
That's no reason to commit terrorism!

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:36.030
Were you really going to attack the mayor?

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:39.610
The bomb is a fake. It's not lethal.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:43.450
But nobody will listen
unless you scare them.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.450
I don't trust civil servants.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:48.790
So what will you do now?

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.750
I only want to protect this town.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:53.960
Get out. Right now.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:57.380
You haven't done anything wrong yet.

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:01.890
Young lady.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:08.390
These are my comrades-in-arms who fought
and died in the war and for our rights.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.100
If this is a city for beastmen,

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:14.310
then I want their graves to be built here.

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.900
Tell the mayor that.

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:21.070
I'll tell her. I swear it.

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:25.620
Oh, right. I'm not the only one
who flew into this city.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.200
There's one more.

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:31.080
<i>There's only one guy</i>
<i>who could fly that fast.</i>

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:34.210
In the underworld, he's called Meteor.

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:38.670
He's an assassin who is willing to do
anything for a price. Watch out.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:40.670
Is he after the mayor?

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:43.890
No. If he were, I would have noticed.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:45.970
Then it must be...

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:51.390
Chairman, it's dangerous to go out there.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:55.270
Maybe so. But it only makes it worse
if I run and hide.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.420
We're too late!

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.250
What's that?

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:16.460
Can you fly again?

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:39.900
Behold! A winged Silver Wolf!

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:42.860
Her grace is not only for beastmen,

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:45.110
but is showered generously
on humans as well!

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:48.950
Our founder, Déesse Louve,

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:53.540
is truly the savior of the beastman world!

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.670
You blew it, so give it up.

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:24.440
Listen to the voice of the citizens!

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:28.570
Can you ignore their voices,
Alan Sylvasta?

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.830
What a pain this has become.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:40.880
Wow!

00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:43.340
You're amazing, Nazuna!

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:50.490
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
